{title: Dare to Be a Daniel}
{artist: Philip P. Bliss}
{genre: Children, Gospel}
{style: Traditional}
{flow: Response}
{key: G}
{tempo: 112}
{time: 4/4}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[G]Standing by a purpose true
[D]Heeding God's command
[G]Honor them, the faithful few
[D]All hail to Daniel's [G]band
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
[G]Dare to be a Daniel
[D]Dare to stand alone
[G]Dare to have a purpose firm
[D]Dare to make it [G]known
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[G]Many mighty men are lost
[D]Daring not to stand
[G]Who for God had been a host
[D]By joining Daniel's [G]band
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[G]Many giants, great and tall
[D]Stalking through the land
[G]Headlong to the earth would fall
[D]If met by Daniel's [G]band
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[G]Hold the Gospel banner high
[D]On to victory grand
[G]Satan and his hosts defy
[D]And shout for Daniel's [G]band
{end_of_verse}
